From 6798d43d71bdd6ab7205224ce998287511f7b42b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:13:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] erofs: consume signed metadata with fail-closed
 lifecycle

Rebase the signed EROFS ingestion and lifecycle hardening on the current
Azure Linux 3.0-dev containerd baseline (ae153a06b).

Consume signed precomputed EROFS metadata and Merkle trees, retain the
selected referrer graph, bind committed snapshots to the selected root
hash and signature, and fail closed when signed state is incomplete or
contradictory. Keep ordinary overlayfs and unsigned EROFS behavior
unchanged.

Use root-scoped mapper names and keyed lifecycle locks through mount and
cleanup. Validate existing signed tables before reuse, recreate invalid
zero-open mappings, and remove mappings on final unmount or snapshot
removal. Deliberately omit the optional idle mapper cache, restart
reconciliation, supplemental-group cache, pagination, and CRI cache
refresh; the latter two follow as isolated commits.

Keep local formatting reproducible with a deterministic dm-verity UUID,
select equal-timestamp referrers deterministically, and account for
separate Merkle trees and sidecars in committed snapshot usage.

Tests and standalone documentation remain out of the production carry and
will be maintained on the companion validation branch.

